<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.8.3: Understanding That the Quadratic Formula Is the Combined Steps of Completing the Square</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02466</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.8.3: Understanding That the Quadratic Formula Is the Combined Steps of Completing the Square</md:title>
    <md:uuid>15324b4e-953c-4b45-989c-71ab982a99ea</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
          <para id="para-00001">Here is one solution for solving <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> by <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">completing the square</term>, where each step is shown, but numerical expressions are not evaluated.</para>
          <para id="para-00002">Original equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00003"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00004"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00006"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00007"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00008"><emphasis>Step 6</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00009"><emphasis>Step 7</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00010"><emphasis>Step 8</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00011"><emphasis>Step 9</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00012"><emphasis>Step 10</emphasis> - </para><para id="para-00029"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <exercise id="exer-00001">
            <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00013">In Step 2, the equation is multiplied by 4. Why might that be?</para>
          <para id="para-00014"></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00015">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00016">To make the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">perfect square</term> and the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> an even number</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00017">In Step 5, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is added to each side. Why might that be?</para>
          <para id="para-00018"></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00020"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> completes the square for the expression on the left side. To keep the two sides equal, it needs to be added to the other side as well.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00021">What happened between Step 5 and Step 6?</para>
          <para id="para-00022"></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00023">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00024">The perfect square is rewritten in factored form, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is rewritten as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title id="para-00025">Building Character: Intellectual Humility</title>

  <media alt="Two people stand at podiums, engaged in a debate. Both wear suits with rosette pins and speak animatedly. Speech bubbles with question marks and ellipses hover above them. Balloons and plants decorate the scene.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_10_08_01.png" width="200px"/>
          </media>

            <para id="para-00026">No matter how old you are, with intellectual humility you become wiser. It helps you be less judgmental of others, learn more in school, and be a better leader.</para>
            <para id="para-00027">Think about yourself. Are these statements true for you?</para>
            <list id="list-00001">
          <item>I recognize the value in opinions that are different from my own. </item>
          <item>I accept that my beliefs and attitudes may be wrong. </item>
        </list>
            <para id="para-00028">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
